			"width": 1781.4957275390625,
			"height": 1305,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1971c2",
			"backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 4,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 2,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bDo",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 404854856,
			"version": 1347,
			"versionNonce": 1655561016,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1734444049904,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Fault Tolerance\nInternal SLAs\nBackup Types\n - Full Everything in the backup policy is backed up\n - Incremental Anything changed since the last backup is backed up, the archive bit is cleared\n - Differential Anything changed since the last full backup is backed up, the archive bit is not cleared\n - copy a full backup, but don't clear the archive bit.\nBackups policy\n- what to, what not to\n- how long to keep\nArchive bit: a flag indicates if the file was changed since the last full or incremental backup.\n\nRAID: Redundant Array of Independent/Inexpensive Disks\n- RAID 0: no mirroring or parity, only provide faster R/W, >=2disks\n- RAID 1: Mirror set, 2 disks with identical data\n- RAID 5: combined speed with redundancy, >=3 disks\n\nSystem Redundancy\nservers: redundant PSU (Power supply unit) and NICs\nredundant disk controllers\napplication, deploy as clusters, load balancing\n\nDatabase Shadowing\n- Exact real time copy (another location)\n\nElectronic Vaulting: Remote backup service\n\nRemote Journaling: sends transaction log files to a remote location\n",
			"fontSize": 36,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "NR7_qd73gBM37-cD8c_SH",
			"originalText": "Fault Tolerance\nInternal SLAs\nBackup Types\n - Full Everything in the backup policy is backed up\n - Incremental Anything changed since the last backup is backed up, the archive bit is cleared\n - Differential Anything changed since the last full backup is backed up, the archive bit is not cleared\n - copy a full backup, but don't clear the archive bit.\nBackups policy\n- what to, what not to\n- how long to keep\nArchive bit: a flag indicates if the file was changed since the last full or incremental backup.\n\nRAID: Redundant Array of Independent/Inexpensive Disks\n- RAID 0: no mirroring or parity, only provide faster R/W, >=2disks\n- RAID 1: Mirror set, 2 disks with identical data\n- RAID 5: combined speed with redundancy, >=3 disks\n\nSystem Redundancy\nservers: redundant PSU (Power supply unit) and NICs\nredundant disk controllers\napplication, deploy as clusters, load balancing\n\nDatabase Shadowing\n- Exact real time copy (another location)\n\nElectronic Vaulting: Remote backup service\n\nRemote Journaling: sends transaction log files to a remote location\n",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"created": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "",
			"labelPosition": null,
			"baseFontSize": null
		},
