		{
			"id": "ZXYSM0gn",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 16973.317927095643,
			"y": 5050.56041758792,
			"width": 1199.411865234375,
			"height": 2655,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1971c2",
			"backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 4,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 2,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bE3V",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 979880713,
			"version": 1689,
			"versionNonce": 1201825065,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1734445610692,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "BIA Business Impact Analysis\nRPO: Recovery Point Objective\nthe acceptable amount of data that can not be recovered\nMTD Maximum Tolerable Downtime >= RTO+WRT\n\nMAD: Maximum Allowable Downtime\nMAO: Maximum Acceptable Outage\nMTPoD: Maximum Tolerable Period of Disruption\nRTO: Recovery Time Objective\nWRT: Work Recovery Time\nMTBF: Mean Time Between Failures\nMTTR: Mean Time to Repair\nMOR: Minimum Operation Requirements\n\nRecovery Strategies\n- Supply Chain\n- Infrastructure 不光是自己公司要恢复，相关方，基础水电煤气也要恢复\n1) Redundant Site\n2) Hot Site\n3) Warm Site\n4) Cold Site\n5) Reciprocal Agreement Site\n6) Mobile Site\n7) Subscription/Cloud Site\n\nBCP Related Plan\nCOOP: Continuity of Operation Plan\nCyber Incident Response Team\nOEP: Occupant Emergency Plan\nBRP: Business Recovery Plan\nContinuity of Support Plan\nCMP: The Crisis Management Plan\nCrisis Communication Plan\nCall Trees\nOff Site Copies and Plans\nEOC: Emergency Operations Center\nMOU/MOA Memorandum of Understanding/Agreement\nExecutive Succession Planning\nEmployee Redundancy\n\nTesting the Plans\n1) Simulated Tests\nDRP Review, Read-Through (Checklist)\n3)Walk/Talk-through \n4)Simulation Test (Drill)\n\n\nPhysical Tests\n1)Parallel Processing\n2)Partial Interruption\n3)Full Interruption\n\nTesting\nDrills\nAuditing by 3rd Party\n\nTraining for the plans\nImproving the plans at least once per year\n",
			"fontSize": 36,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "7sVwLs_KwUFWeqOrShWRX",
			"originalText": "BIA Business Impact Analysis\nRPO: Recovery Point Objective\nthe acceptable amount of data that can not be recovered\nMTD Maximum Tolerable Downtime >= RTO+WRT\n\nMAD: Maximum Allowable Downtime\nMAO: Maximum Acceptable Outage\nMTPoD: Maximum Tolerable Period of Disruption\nRTO: Recovery Time Objective\nWRT: Work Recovery Time\nMTBF: Mean Time Between Failures\nMTTR: Mean Time to Repair\nMOR: Minimum Operation Requirements\n\nRecovery Strategies\n- Supply Chain\n- Infrastructure 不光是自己公司要恢复，相关方，基础水电煤气也要恢复\n1) Redundant Site\n2) Hot Site\n3) Warm Site\n4) Cold Site\n5) Reciprocal Agreement Site\n6) Mobile Site\n7) Subscription/Cloud Site\n\nBCP Related Plan\nCOOP: Continuity of Operation Plan\nCyber Incident Response Team\nOEP: Occupant Emergency Plan\nBRP: Business Recovery Plan\nContinuity of Support Plan\nCMP: The Crisis Management Plan\nCrisis Communication Plan\nCall Trees\nOff Site Copies and Plans\nEOC: Emergency Operations Center\nMOU/MOA Memorandum of Understanding/Agreement\nExecutive Succession Planning\nEmployee Redundancy\n\nTesting the Plans\n1) Simulated Tests\nDRP Review, Read-Through (Checklist)\n3)Walk/Talk-through \n4)Simulation Test (Drill)\n\n\nPhysical Tests\n1)Parallel Processing\n2)Partial Interruption\n3)Full Interruption\n\nTesting\nDrills\nAuditing by 3rd Party\n\nTraining for the plans\nImproving the plans at least once per year\n",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"created": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": "",
			"labelPosition": null,
			"baseFontSize": null
		},
