		{
			"id": "6vGTm8Ni",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1008.0800353080631,
			"y": 4844.96524355172,
			"width": 988.9317016601562,
			"height": 1470,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#e03131",
			"backgroundColor": "#ffec99",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "bEc",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1101864609,
			"version": 4714,
			"versionNonce": 1023790209,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1735286149831,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Virtualization and Distributed Computing\nVirtualization benefits\n- cost less\n- easier to stand up new servers\n- back up servers with snapshots\n- build servers with images\n\nHypervisor\ncontrols the access between virtual guest and host \n- Type 1 (Barer Metal) runs on top of the host hardware (Data Center)\n- Type 2 runs on top of a regular OS like Win10 (PC)\n\nVM Escape\n\nHypervisor Security\n\nResource Exhaustion\n\nCloud Computing\n- Private ~\n- Public ~\n- Hybrid ~\n- Community ~\n\nIaaS, PaaS, SaaS\n\nGrid Computing\nmake use of resources not currently in use from 100 or 100000s PCs\n\nP2P Peer to Peer\nany system can be a client/or server\n\nThin Clients\n- Diskless Workstation\n- Thin Client Applications via web browser to connect app on a server\n\nDistributed systems\nDCE: Distributed computing environment\n\nHPC High-Performance Computing systems\n\nEdge computing-systems",
			"fontSize": 28,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "TsG8HChfJXPHzCBwyUhIS",
			"originalText": "Virtualization and Distributed Computing\nVirtualization benefits\n- cost less\n- easier to stand up new servers\n- back up servers with snapshots\n- build servers with images\n\nHypervisor\ncontrols the access between virtual guest and host \n- Type 1 (Barer Metal) runs on top of the host hardware (Data Center)\n- Type 2 runs on top of a regular OS like Win10 (PC)\n\nVM Escape\n\nHypervisor Security\n\nResource Exhaustion\n\nCloud Computing\n- Private ~\n- Public ~\n- Hybrid ~\n- Community ~\n\nIaaS, PaaS, SaaS\n\nGrid Computing\nmake use of resources not currently in use from 100 or 100000s PCs\n\nP2P Peer to Peer\nany system can be a client/or server\n\nThin Clients\n- Diskless Workstation\n- Thin Client Applications via web browser to connect app on a server\n\nDistributed systems\nDCE: Distributed computing environment\n\nHPC High-Performance Computing systems\n\nEdge computing-systems",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"created": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
