			"locked": false,
			"text": "Quantum Key Distribution (QKD)\n- Process\n- Security principles\n- Real-time detection of tampering or\neavesdropping\nChallenges\n- distance limitations\n- cost and complexity\npotential solutions\n- quantum repeaters\n- satellite-based QKDs\n\nCryptographic Attacks\n- Steal the key\n- Brute force\n- key stretching\n- digraph attack\n- man-in-the-middle attack\n- session hijacking (TCP session Hijacking)\n- Social Engineering\n- Rainbow tables\n- known plaintext\n- chosen plaintext\n- adaptive chosen plaintext\n- meet-in-the-middle\n- know key\n- differential cryptanalysis\n- linear cryptanalysis\n- differential linear cryptanalysis\n- Side Channel Attacks\n- Implementation Attack\n- Key Clustering\n- Pass the Hash\n- Kerberos exploitation\n    - overpass the hash\n    - pass the ticket\n    - silver the ticket\n    - golden ticket\n    - Kerberos brute-force\n    - ASREPRoast\n    - Kerberoasting\n- Fault injection\n\nImplementing Cryptography\n- PKI\n- Key Escrow\n- Digital Signatures (for Integrity and Non-\nrepudiation)\n- Digital certificates\n    * CA\n    * ORA \n    * CRL\n    * OCSP\nMAC: Message Authentication Code\nHMAC: Hashed Message Authentication Code\nSSL and TLS\nIPSEC\n    - AH\n    - ESP\n    - SA Security Association\n    - ISAKMP \n    - Tunnel Mode\n    - Transport Mode\n    - IKE\nPretty Good Privacy (PGP)\nMIME Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions\n",
